      <h2 style="font: 600 var(--type-display-2)/1.08 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.025em; margin: 0 0 40px; color: #A8FF45; text-wrap: balance">Common questions about the 2026 standard</h2>
      
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:28px 40px">
        <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(244,248,244,.12);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:#F4F8F4">What is new in the 2026 edition?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:#A9BFAE;margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Four categories are new or newly standalone: Business Logic Errors, Flash Loan Attacks, Proxy and Upgrade Vulnerabilities, and Price Oracle Manipulation promoted to SC02. Each crossed the $100M individual loss threshold in 2025.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(244,248,244,.12);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:#F4F8F4">How does it differ from the 2025 edition?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:#A9BFAE;margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Insecure Randomness dropped out of the top 10, Oracle Manipulation moved from SC07 to SC02, and Logic Errors was split into a broader Business Logic Errors category covering protocol economics and governance.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(244,248,244,.12);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:#F4F8F4">How was the list developed?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:#A9BFAE;margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">From incident data rather than theory. Web3HackHub catalogued 134 documented 2025 incidents with root-cause classification and $3.67B in attributed losses, and the SolidityScan corpus supplied the frequency baseline.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(244,248,244,.12);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:#F4F8F4">Does a CredShields audit cover all ten categories?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:#A9BFAE;margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Yes. Every audit maps findings to the OWASP Smart Contract Top 10 categories, and the report states coverage explicitly.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(244,248,244,.12);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:#F4F8F4">Do regulators and institutions use it?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:#A9BFAE;margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Institutional auditors and exchange listing reviews increasingly reference the OWASP Smart Contract Top 10 in due diligence checklists. It is not itself a regulation.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(244,248,244,.12);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:#F4F8F4">How should development teams use it?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:#A9BFAE;margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">As a design-time checklist and a review gate, not a post-deployment audit substitute. Map each category to a control in your own codebase and test for it before you ship.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(244,248,244,.12);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:#F4F8F4">Can tools map findings to the 2026 Top 10?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:#A9BFAE;margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Yes. SolidityScan maps every finding to its OWASP Smart Contract Top 10 category automatically, which is how the frequency data behind the ranking was produced.</p>
